---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReportIssue from "../components/ReportIssue.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MiniTool HQ — Private Browser Tools for Creators & Sellers"
  description="Private browser tools for creators and sellers. Files stay on your device — marketplace prep, asset cleanup, and more jobs without uploading."
>
  <section class="hero-home">
    <p class="badge">Private · In-browser · No upload</p>
    <p class="brand-mark">MiniTool HQ</p>
    <h1>Private tools for creators &amp; sellers.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Focused browser tools that keep files on your device. Pick a job below and go.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="tools" class="section tools-first">
    <h2>Tools</h2>
    <div class="tool-cards">
      <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/amazon-image-prep">
        <h2>Amazon Image Prep</h2>
        <p>
          Batch resize to ~2000px, optional white background, strip EXIF/GPS, ZIP download. No
          upload.
        </p>
      </a>
      <div class="tool-card" style="opacity: 0.55; cursor: default;">
        <h2>Image Compressor</h2>
        <p>Coming next — private batch compression.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="value" class="section value-block">
    <h2>Why this exists</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Generic free editors already cover “edit any image privately.” MiniTool HQ is for
      <strong>specific jobs</strong> — marketplace listings, creator assets, seller ops — with
      the right defaults, without uploading files to a random server.
    </p>
    <div class="value-grid">
      <div class="value-item">
        <h3>Job-first, not toolbox-first</h3>
        <p>
          One clear workflow per tool — not a 100-feature swiss army knife. More vertical tools
          land on this same site over time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-item">
        <h3>Private by design</h3>
        <p>
          Processing runs in your browser. Your files are not uploaded to our servers for editing.
          Trust the Network tab, not a slogan alone.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-item">
        <h3>Seller &amp; creator workflows</h3>
        <p>
          Built for people shipping listings and assets: clear specs, batch-friendly steps, and
          room to grow beyond any single marketplace.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-item">
        <h3>Free to use for core work</h3>
        <p>
          Open a tool and go — no account required for core use. Optional higher limits stay out of
          the way until you need them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReportIssue />
</BaseLayout>
